    <p class="draft-banner"><strong>Draft for organizational and legal review.</strong> This code is not yet approved for production use and does not constitute legal advice.</p>
    <h1>CHAIC Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p><strong>Draft last updated:</strong> July 24, 2026</p>
    <p>CHAIC is committed to a professional, inclusive, accessible, and safe event where people can exchange ideas about healthcare and artificial intelligence. This draft applies to attendees, speakers, sponsors, exhibitors, vendors, volunteers, organizers, and staff.</p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>The code applies in all CHAIC-controlled spaces, including conference and workshop rooms, exhibit areas, networking events, social functions, online event spaces, direct event communications, and conduct connected to participation in CHAIC.</p>

    <h2>Expected conduct</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Treat people with respect, dignity, and professional courtesy.</li>
      <li>Welcome different backgrounds, disciplines, experiences, identities, and viewpoints.</li>
      <li>Communicate disagreement constructively and avoid personal attacks.</li>
      <li>Respect privacy, confidentiality, consent, intellectual property, and photography preferences.</li>
      <li>Follow venue, safety, accessibility, and event-staff instructions.</li>
      <li>Discuss clinical cases only with appropriate de-identification and authorization; never expose protected health information.</li>
      <li>Disclose relevant commercial relationships or conflicts when presenting claims or products.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prohibited behavior</h2>
    <p>Harassment, discrimination, intimidation, stalking, threats, violence, unwanted sexual attention, deliberate misgendering, sustained disruption, retaliation, and abusive or demeaning conduct are prohibited. So are unauthorized recording, disclosure of confidential or patient information, unsafe demonstrations, possession of prohibited items, and marketing practices that ignore attendee consent or event rules.</p>

    <h2>Reporting concerns</h2>
    <p>If you experience or witness concerning conduct, contact a clearly identified CHAIC staff member or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Confidential%20Code%20of%20Conduct%20Report">{{ site.email }}</a>. The final approved code should add an event-day phone number, named response leads, a private reporting location, and an alternate contact when the concern involves an organizer.</p>
    <p>Reports should include, when safe and possible, what happened, when and where it occurred, the people involved, witnesses, and any immediate safety needs. CHAIC should limit information to those who need it to assess and respond, while recognizing that complete confidentiality cannot always be guaranteed.</p>

    <h2>Response and enforcement</h2>
    <p>CHAIC may take steps proportionate to the circumstances, including a warning, facilitated separation, session removal, revocation of event access without refund, sponsor or speaker action, venue security involvement, or referral to emergency services or law enforcement. A response should consider immediate safety, available information, fairness, privacy, and anti-retaliation obligations.</p>

    <h2>Accessibility and accommodations</h2>
    <p>Participants should not obstruct accessible routes, mobility devices, captioning, interpretation, service animals, sensory needs, or approved accommodations. Request event-specific support at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=CHAIC%20accessibility%20request">{{ site.email }}</a> as early as possible.</p>

    <h2>Emergencies</h2>
    <p>For an immediate threat or medical emergency, call 911 and alert Puerto Rico Convention Center security or CHAIC staff. Do not use the conduct-reporting email as an emergency channel.</p>

    <h2>Review before approval</h2>
    <p>The organization should confirm reporting personnel, response procedures, venue coordination, refund implications, record retention, confidentiality language, and applicable Puerto Rico and federal law before publication.</p>
